│▊▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▎││ Introduction                                                  │▏           ← Move cursor left
│▊  Search...                            ▎││╸━━━━━━━━━━━━╺━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━│▏           → Move cursor right or accept the
│▊▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▎││                                                               │▏             completion suggestion
│                                         ││                                                               │▏     home ^a Go to start
│ ★  Owner       Name         Private     ││         LazyGithub: A Terminal UI For GitHub (0.6.6)          │▏      end ^e Go to end
│ ☆  parity-bot  dotfiles     ✘           ││                                                               │▏        pgup Page Up
│ ☆  parity-bot  hello-world  ✘           ││  LazyGithub is a terminal UI for interacting with GitHub.     │▏        pgdn Page Down
│ ☆  parity-bot  lazy-demo    ✘           ││  You can get started by selecting one of the repositories     │▏       ^pgup Page Left
│                                         ││  listed in the table on the left. Once you have selected a    │▏       ^pgdn Page Right
│                                         ││  repository, any issues, pull requests, and action workflows  │▏     shift+← Move cursor left and select
│                                         ││  will be retrieved and displayed below it.                    │▏          ^← Move cursor left a word
│                                         ││                                                               │▏    shift+^← Move cursor left a word and select
│                                         ││  Issues, pull requests, and action lists can also be          │▏     shift+→ Move cursor right and select
│                                         ││  interacted with!                                             │▏          ^→ Move cursor right a word
│                                         ││                                                               │▏    shift+^→ Move cursor right a word and select
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘│                                                               │▏           ⌫ Delete character left
┌─ [2] Pull Requests ─────────────────────┐│  Pull Requests                                                │▏    shift+^a Select all
│ #  Status  Author  Title                ││                                                               │▏  shift+home Select line start
│                                         ││  You can interact with a PR by viewing its details, viewing   │▏   shift+end Select line end
│                                         ││  the PR diff, and participating in any active conversations   │▏      del ^d Delete character right
│                                         ││  happening on the PR. You can also create a new PR for the    │▏           ⏎ Submit
│                                         ││  currently selected repo.                                     │▏          ^w Delete left to start of word
│                                         ││                                                               │▏          ^u Delete all to the left
│                                         ││                                                               │▏          ^f Delete right to start of word
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘│  Issues                                                       │▏          ^k Delete all to the right
┌─ [3] Issues ────────────────────────────┐│                                                               │▏          ^x Cut selected text
│ #  Status  Author  Title                ││  You can interact with an issue by viewing its details,       │▏  ^c super+c Copy selected text
│                                         ││  partipcating in any activate conversations happening on the  │▏          ^v Paste text from the clipboard
│                                         ││  issue, and by editing the issue itself. This means that you  │▏
│                                         ││  can close an issue from within LazyGithub.                   │▏           / Search Search in the table
│                                         ││                                                               │▏
│                                         ││                                                               │▏         tab Focus Next
│                                         ││  Actions                                                      │▏   shift+tab Focus Previous
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘│                                                               │▏          ^n Notifications Open the notifications
┌─ [4] Workflows ─────────────────────────┐│  Github action and workflow support is pretty limited. It     │▏             modal
│ Time  Result  Job Name  Run Name  Run # ││  currently only supports listing the workflows and the most   │▏
│                                         ││  recent runs across all actions on the currently selected     │▏          ^q Quit Quit the app and return to the
│                                         ││  repo, as well as kicking off a workflow that supports        │▏             command prompt.
│                                         ││  manual triggers.                                             │▏          ^p Command Pallete
│                                         ││                                                               │▏
│                                         ││                                                               │▏
│                                         ││                                                               │▏
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘▏
 / Search  ^p Command Pallete                                                                               ▏
